# port-patches.sh: glm/sampling-r7 @ 6cc5c62a69ae over glm/zig-engine-fixes-on-186 @ e027c49cd06d (commits fe2f060f7929..0e0518f341f2); regenerate with scripts/port-patches.sh, do not edit
glm_cuda: decode clusters, draft prelaunch and narrow prompt tiles (TF_GLM_QMM_CLUSTERS, TF_GLM_DRAFT_PRELAUNCH, TF_GLM_PROMPT_TILE; after BadAd84's GLM 0103, 0100, 0102)

Each byte-identical by design and behind its own switch; their speed at TP=2 is measured on the GPU, not assumed.

Commits:
- glm_cuda: decode K splits sum in a cluster only past 64 rows or from 28 Mi weight values (TF_GLM_QMM_CLUSTERS, port of BadAd84's GLM 0103)
- glm_cuda: the DFlash2 block pass queues behind the round's tap pass with no wait between (TF_GLM_DRAFT_PRELAUNCH, after BadAd84's GLM 0100)
- glm_cuda: narrow prompt projections on 64 x 64 tiles (TF_GLM_PROMPT_TILE, port of BadAd84's GLM 0102)

Credits: Robert Wojciechowski (GitHub @wojo, X @rwojo).
Apply from the checkout root with: git apply 0032-zig-glm-decode-speed.patch

